    <name>
      <text>Permutations I - Evaluating nPr</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Evaluate \(_{ {@pn@} }P_{ {@pr@} }\).</p>
<p>\(_{ {@pn@} }P_{ {@pr@} } = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) Evaluate \(_{ {@pn2@} }P_{ {@pr2@} }\).</p>
<p>\(_{ {@pn2@} }P_{ {@pr2@} } = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>\(_{ {@pn@} }P_{ {@pr@} } = \dfrac{ {@pn@}!}{({@pn@}-{@pr@})!} = \dfrac{ {@pn@}!}{ {@pn-pr@}!}\), which expands to the product of \({@pr@}\) descending numbers starting at \({@pn@}\), giving \({@pans1@}\).</p>
<p>\(_{ {@pn2@} }P_{ {@pr2@} } = \dfrac{ {@pn2@}!}{({@pn2@}-{@pr2@})!} = \dfrac{ {@pn2@}!}{ {@pn2-pr2@}!}\), which expands to the product of \({@pr2@}\) descending numbers starting at \({@pn2@}\), giving \({@pans2@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
